## 4.  Quick recap of important concepts

| Feature | What it is | Why it matters |
|---------|------------|----------------|
| `class` | Data + functions grouped | Encapsulates behaviour |
| `public/protected/private` | Access control | Controls visibility |
| `:` (colon) after class name | Inheritance | Re‑use code |
| `virtual` | Polymorphic dispatch | Runtime selection of derived implementation |
| `= 0` after a virtual function | Pure virtual | Makes the class abstract |
| `override` | Keyword after derived function | Compiler checks that you actually override a base method |
| `virtual ~Base() = default;` | Virtual destructor | Ensures derived destructors run when deleting through a base pointer |
| `protected` data | Accessible to derived | Allows derived classes to use base data without exposing it publicly |

